    "intro": "I am Sriram, a computer science student at Stevens Institute of Technology, class of 2028. I work mostly on backends and data: this summer I was a data engineering intern at Bloom Value Corporation, building ETL views on Microsoft Fabric, a clinical document pipeline, and an HL7 FHIR integration that passed all four federal conformance submissions. I co-founded Sponge, an AI-native technical assessment platform, and since 2023 I have built and run ISNNetwork, a revenue-generating game server for advanced players. My hackathon project Morphexis, which measures epistemic drift in news coverage, placed in the top 7 of 188 teams at RAISE-26.\n\nOff the keyboard I was a three-time state placer in high school wrestling, swam competitively for ten years, and was selected for the national round of the Darien Young Composers competition on piano. I also lift, climb, and play chess (1850 on chess.com, 1600 FIDE).",
